WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:06.060
Every so often, the Foundation gets a tip
about an anomalous object rather than discovering

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.950
it through their global surveillance network.

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:14.190
Tip-offs aren’t common, because few people
know how to even get in contact with the Foundation

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.750
directly, but when they do, it’s always
a relief.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.789
The agents and Mobile Task Forces that are
sent to investigate and retrieve possible

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:27.730
SCPs usually walk in blind - there’s no
telling what they might find.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:32.980
But when a tip-off, report, or informant from
one of the Groups of Interest comes in and

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:38.289
spills the beans, the brave front-liners of
the Foundation usually have a slightly better

00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:42.020
idea of what they’re tackling.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.170
Usually.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.989
Sometimes they get complacent and end up underestimating
or going in underprepared.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:50.820
And when that happens…

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.579
well, the consequences can be disastrous.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:01:00.719
Way back in 1990, the Foundation received
an unexpected tip-off from one of its contacts

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:03.179
based on the island of Hong Kong.

00:01:03.179 --> 00:01:08.900
It wasn’t much - just a location and a general
description of the effects told discreetly

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.270
over the phone.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:15.610
The contact was one of some fifty thousand
Chinese residents of a particular neighborhood

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.960
in Hong Kong – the infamous Kowloon Walled
City.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.820
The city was originally a Chinese military
fort on the island of Hong Kong.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:29.550
When the island was sold to the British Empire
at the end of the 19th century, the fort was

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:35.590
converted into massive, densely packed apartment
buildings and quickly became an enclave for

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:36.980
the Chinese.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:42.380
When Japan occupied Hong Kong during WW2,
tens of thousands of ethnic Chinese on the

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:46.170
island took refuge in the massive apartment
blocks of the slum.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:52.510
There was no government, no police, no laws
– the dozens of floors were controlled by

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:56.940
gangs and drug dealers, but it was better
than being homeless.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:02.190
And of course, the residents were incredibly
suspicious of any authorities.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:07.790
You can imagine why the Foundation was reticent
to send some of their best men into a densely-packed

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:12.370
civilian area that was likely to be hostile
to their presence.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:17.910
Their contact informed them that the anomalous
object was a small relic of some kind with

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.240
strange, terrifying powers.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:25.290
It was located deep in the heart of the Walled
City, and it might even be responsible for

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.070
the very city’s existence.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:34.010
Foundation command considered that the alternative
was letting fifty-thousand people reside inside

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:39.360
of an uncontained anomaly, and decided that
they’d send someone to investigate.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.920
They picked troops from Mobile Task Force
Zeta-9, the Mole Rats.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.040
The Mole Rats are some of the Foundation’s
most trustworthy operatives – they’re

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:55.050
a task force specially trained and equipped
to operate in dangerous and anomalous environments,

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.470
particularly those that are underground or
underwater.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:03.310
Whether it’s an undersea cave system or
an endless, claustrophobic basement, the Mole

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:09.650
Rats perform search, rescue, containment,
and even recovery in these terrifying places.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:14.800
They seemed like the natural fit to be the
ones to lead the expedition, while exploring

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.330
and finding out what in the world had caused
the Kowloon Walled City.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:27.250
The team landed in Hong Kong on June 3rd,
led by one Gordon Richards, a member of Zeta-9.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:33.290
He kept an extensive personal diary, as most
agents do - and from it, the Foundation was

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:37.590
able to learn what SCP-184 truly was.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:42.000
The first impression Richards had of the Walled
City while exploring it with his partner,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.230
Henry, was pure disgust.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:50.000
It was a densely-packed slum that was largely
made of trash and refuse, covered in filth

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.480
and stinking to high heaven.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.320
The suits that the team wore protected them
from any hazardous material or danger, but

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:03.209
it was still a vile experience moving through
the cramped streets and corridors of the ghetto.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:08.150
At one point, Richards’ partner was walking
through an area piled knee-deep in trash when

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:11.970
the floor gave out, dumping him into a cesspool.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.280
On their first day, they learned practically
nothing from the locals.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.599
The residents of the Walled City were suspicious
of outsiders.

00:04:19.599 --> 00:04:25.520
They’d either avoid the agents or throw
trash and insults at them from afar in Cantonese

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.080
and sometimes Mandarin.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.789
But Richards did manage to catch whispers
in some of the bars that peppered the city

00:04:31.789 --> 00:04:37.750
– there was something strange in the center
of the mass, something that sounded nothing

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.999
short of anomalous.

00:04:39.999 --> 00:04:42.629
Foundation agents assisted Hong Kong Police
Officers

00:04:42.629 --> 00:04:46.789
in conducting raids overnight, hoping to find
more information.

00:04:46.789 --> 00:04:51.099
In the morning, the Mole Rats returned to
investigate, and found the first evidence

00:04:51.099 --> 00:04:56.460
of something actually anomalous affecting
several of the tiny apartments.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:01.319
From the outside, they looked like the same
ragged shanties as the other hundred-square-foot

00:05:01.319 --> 00:05:04.840
apartments, but they were far too big from
the inside.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:09.879
Henry had seemed spooked since his fall into
the cesspit the day prior - the other agents

00:05:09.879 --> 00:05:14.699
tried talking to him but it didn’t help
much, and he spent most of the day in a strange

00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:17.280
fugue, muttering to himself.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:22.699
Richards told him to knock it off, but never
reported it, feeling bad for the new kid.

00:05:22.699 --> 00:05:27.360
The next day would be spent in the sewers,
trying to find a direct route to the center

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.789
of the city where this object was being held.

00:05:30.789 --> 00:05:35.960
Richards went into the sewer with a fellow
agent but found nothing except more waste

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.090
and filth.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:41.689
They were unable to get on the radio with
the rest of the team inside the actual building

00:05:41.689 --> 00:05:47.689
until they came out early the next day, after
spending almost a full day underground.

00:05:47.689 --> 00:05:52.300
They were quickly pulled out by other agents
and briefed: while they had been in the sewers,

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:56.530
Henry and another agent had been exploring
the central portion of the city, That’s

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:59.249
when they were rushed by an angry mob.

00:05:59.249 --> 00:06:03.650
Dozens of people attacked before they even
had a chance to retaliate – both were viciously

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:09.580
beaten, but Henry was dragged off deeper into
the city and the other agent was injured during

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:11.620
his retreat back to base.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:16.119
When they could no longer hear Henry’s screams
on the radio, several armed agents rushed

00:06:16.119 --> 00:06:17.580
in to extract him.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:20.430
That’s when they heard Henry’s radio again.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:25.259
He was screaming and rambling incoherently,
sounding like he was hallucinating about the

00:06:25.259 --> 00:06:28.639
city being alive when the radio cut out again.

00:06:28.639 --> 00:06:33.460
The search team was shocked by the sight of
Henry rounding the corner, running at full

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.779
pace and screaming without his helmet.

00:06:35.779 --> 00:06:41.330
He pushed an agent aside before smashing right
through one of the weak, thin garbage walls,

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.360
falling six stories onto a pile of metal scrap.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:49.330
The sight was gruesome, and it took them hours
to recover his body.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:54.499
Zeta-9 was done screwing around - they were
going to round up the city’s leaders and

00:06:54.499 --> 00:06:58.249
find this anomaly before it killed anyone
else.

00:06:58.249 --> 00:07:03.899
Over the next day or so, the agents, aided
by the Hong Kong PD, rounded up many of the

00:07:03.899 --> 00:07:09.389
city elders and community leaders, pulling
them from their apartments and shanties.

00:07:09.389 --> 00:07:14.360
Zeta-9 worked on interrogating them for information,
while Richards provided the muscle.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:18.720
The first person they pulled was a member
of the Chinese Triads, one of the gangs that

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.009
functionally ran that city.

00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:26.919
When he didn’t cooperate, the agents broke
his legs, and he suddenly became a lot more

00:07:26.919 --> 00:07:27.919
talkative.

00:07:27.919 --> 00:07:32.939
He explained that the anomaly was called “the
Builder” and no one quite knew where it

00:07:32.939 --> 00:07:35.509
came from or how it worked.

00:07:35.509 --> 00:07:39.729
The closest he had ever come was standing
guard outside rooms while it “worked”,

00:07:39.729 --> 00:07:42.300
and that the city elders would know more.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:45.939
When he brushed off Henry’s death, Richards
broke his jaw.

00:07:45.939 --> 00:07:51.650
The next person was an ancient-looking Chinese
man named Long Wen, one of the city’s reclusive

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:52.669
elders.

00:07:52.669 --> 00:07:58.410
He was indomitable - no matter what Richards
did, he wouldn’t give in under abuse or

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.410
torture.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:04.319
But when one of the agents suggested that
Zeta-9 pay a visit to his family, he immediately

00:08:04.319 --> 00:08:05.610
opened up.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:10.490
He told them that The Builder was kept in
an old temple that the City had grown around.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:15.520
It was highly secret and only a few people
could look upon it without going mad - he

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:20.520
had tried to show Henry so that the Foundation
wouldn’t take it away, but obviously, that

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.550
hadn’t gone quite as planned.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:26.680
When asked where it was, Long-Wen explained
that as soon as the agents had arrived, they

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:31.809
had moved it deep inside the city, where no
one would be able to get to it.

00:08:31.809 --> 00:08:38.110
But Zeta-9 took that as a challenge - tomorrow,
they were moving into the city’s temple,

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:41.550
and not coming out without that anomaly.

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:45.850
Richards and the rest of the Mole Rats prepared
themselves for the expedition over the following

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.100
few days.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:51.620
They were going to venture deep into the heart
of the Kowloon Walled City, far away from

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:54.800
any supply lines or external Foundation support.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:59.690
They made sure they went in heavily armed,
with their suits life-support enabled, and

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:02.410
prepared for every possibility.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:07.110
They departed on June 8th, heading straight
into the belly of the city, where Henry had

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.949
been abducted by the mob.

00:09:08.949 --> 00:09:14.319
At first, it seemed strange but not overtly
anomalous – the same dingy, damp apartments

00:09:14.319 --> 00:09:15.529
full of garbage.

00:09:15.529 --> 00:09:21.769
But eventually, they came upon what they were
looking for – a small, tiny temple, Buddhist

00:09:21.769 --> 00:09:23.440
in style and design.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:28.149
It was made of stone and wood, with a small
Buddha statue out front.

00:09:28.149 --> 00:09:33.089
It was the only thing that looked remotely
out of place, otherwise surrounded by shanties

00:09:33.089 --> 00:09:34.910
and cobbled-together homes.

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:39.690
In the words of the great David Byrne, this
must be the place.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:44.930
At first, it was nothing new – the temple
was too big on the inside, but it was nothing

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:48.899
they hadn’t seen in the hundred other rooms
in this massive building.

00:09:48.899 --> 00:09:53.060
A small shrine, a few seats here and there,
altars.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:58.449
But then Richards and the other agents noticed
something – a sliding door, built into the

00:09:58.449 --> 00:10:01.269
wall of the tiny ten-foot temple.

00:10:01.269 --> 00:10:06.570
It made no sense – a door would exit out
into the apartment right next door.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:12.839
When they opened it, they found… a hallway
leading deeper into the structure, made of

00:10:12.839 --> 00:10:17.380
the same wood and rice paper that the temple
was constructed from.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:22.440
It was long, too – at this point, they should’ve
been deep into the other apartments in the

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:26.829
building, More so than any other room they
had checked before.

00:10:26.829 --> 00:10:31.959
As they travelled down the corridor, they
found more sliding doors lining the walls.

00:10:31.959 --> 00:10:37.790
More temple rooms, altars, and meditation
chambers, all recreated and rearranged by

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:39.050
the anomaly.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:45.360
It was like someone built twelve whole temples
inside this one tiny structure, expanding

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:46.740
ever inward.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:51.250
That must’ve been why they called this thing
the Builder, whatever it was.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:56.199
The Mole Rats knew that this place was bound
to be gigantic, and set up a small base camp

00:10:56.199 --> 00:11:01.120
in the original temple, to stop any of the
residents from getting the jump on them.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:05.920
Then they got their suits sealed, their equipment
rigged up, and went to work exploring the

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:10.949
various corridors, hallways, and temples that
had grown out of this anomaly.

00:11:10.949 --> 00:11:16.259
At first, it was simple and repetitive, but
things started to get strange after the sixth

00:11:16.259 --> 00:11:18.120
hour of exploration.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:23.250
The rooms began to thin out until the Mole
Rats were mostly exploring uninterrupted,

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:26.810
long hallways made of bamboo and rice paper.

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:31.920
They came upon a room with something inside
it – another meditation chamber, but this

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.650
time a small bronze Buddha statue was placed
in the center of the room.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:41.600
It was the size of Richards’ fist, and his
team collected a sample before moving to the

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.100
sliding door at the rear of the room.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:49.250
They opened it up and exited right back into
a meditation room with a tiny, fist-sized

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:50.920
Buddha in the center.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:55.209
For a second, they thought they had been transported
backward, but this Buddha didn’t have any

00:11:55.209 --> 00:11:56.860
samples taken out of it.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:01.350
It was an identical copy of the room they
had just entered through.

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:07.139
Strange, but not unexpected – they didn’t
bother taking a sample and moved to the next

00:12:07.139 --> 00:12:08.139
room.

00:12:08.139 --> 00:12:12.089
Which was also a meditation chamber with a
Buddha in the middle.

00:12:12.089 --> 00:12:16.970
All in all, they found eighty-three rooms
in a row that were identical copies of that

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:21.610
one chamber with the Buddha, connected by
the sliding doors.

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:26.320
After that experience, and a few hallways
later, they came upon another familiar sight

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:32.639
– a perfect recreation of the original altar
room they had entered into the temple from,

00:12:32.639 --> 00:12:34.730
but with one difference.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:39.860
Rather than being made out of planks of wood
and stone, this room seemed to be carved from

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:44.579
a single, massive piece of wood with no seams
or breaks.

00:12:44.579 --> 00:12:49.910
There were no tool marks anywhere, and it
looked as though it’d been somehow naturally

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:50.910
formed.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:55.160
But they did find a small collection of documents,
written in Chinese, in the corner.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:58.850
They scanned the documents and sent digital
copies back to HQ.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:05.370
The agents at the base responded – the anomaly
had been designated SCP-184, and the templegoers

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.689
seemed to think it was a gift from God.

00:13:07.689 --> 00:13:12.380
They allowed people to bring it into their
apartments for a small payment and let it

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:14.259
grow the space.

00:13:14.259 --> 00:13:18.699
Zeta-9 resolved to grab it and get out before
it could expand the temple any further.

00:13:18.699 --> 00:13:21.190
They bunked down for the night to get some
sleep.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:25.200
The next morning, they continued moving through
the temple until they hit a branch in the

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.060
road and split the team.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:30.839
Richards picked one hallway and set out on
his own, climbing upwards.

00:13:30.839 --> 00:13:35.490
The walls in this section of the temple were
irregular – they were undulating, wavy.

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:40.149
The wood and rice had given way to hard stone
hallways.

00:13:40.149 --> 00:13:44.670
Richards slipped into one of the rooms to
rest for a while, and found that all the furniture

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:49.580
was made of beautiful green jade, despite
being wonderfully soft.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:53.120
He rested on the jade bed for a while before
continuing on.

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:57.269
He wrote in the journal that he didn’t feel
well - disconnected from the environment,

00:13:57.269 --> 00:13:59.610
not like a usual mission.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:04.500
One of his team members had died, and the
environment itself felt hostile.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:07.810
Without anyone else to talk to, he was thinking
too much.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:09.480
But it was just nerves.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:11.639
He signed the journal and kept moving.

00:14:11.639 --> 00:14:15.000
For the next hours and days, Richards continued
on.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.310
His suit’s ability to make food and water
was running low.

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:22.449
As he moved through the stone temple, he saw
something out of the corner of his eye that

00:14:22.449 --> 00:14:23.830
wasn’t there when he looked again.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:26.980
He heard voices that couldn’t possibly be
there.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:30.819
He’d been climbing for so long he’d lost
track of time.

00:14:30.819 --> 00:14:36.000
While climbing up the shaft, he finally saw
light and darted through - only to enter a

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:39.629
room filled with lit candles, not sunlight.

00:14:39.629 --> 00:14:44.810
Enraged, he smashed them all with his helmet,
breaking the helmet to pieces.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:49.089
He sat and cried for a while, before dropping
something down the shaft to see how far it

00:14:49.089 --> 00:14:52.209
was to the bottom - but never heard it hit
the floor.

00:14:52.209 --> 00:14:58.970
He set his jaw – Screw containment, he had
to find this thing and utterly destroy it.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:01.290
The next time he saw something, it was days
later.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:06.240
His food and water had run out when he had
found a hall filled with doors lining every

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.240
surface.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:12.680
They all led back into the wall, but he noticed
he was bleeding – the floor wasn’t carpet,

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:18.870
but razor-sharp stone pinpricks that had shredded
the boots of his suit to ribbons, along with

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:19.870
his feet.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.240
He returned to climbing after patching himself
up a little.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.959
He had to kill this thing, somehow.

00:15:24.959 --> 00:15:28.949
The rest of the entries are disparate and
unsigned.

00:15:28.949 --> 00:15:33.889
One of the rare coherent ones revealed that
he was at the top of the shaft, at something

00:15:33.889 --> 00:15:39.740
called the ‘hall to forever’, filled with
light, and that he was ‘going to kill the

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:40.830
heart’.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:45.270
Around the time these entries were written,
the other members of Zeta-9 felt the temple

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:48.300
shaking and cracking, growing unstable.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:53.870
They quickly evacuated, minutes before they
saw the interior of the temple collapsing

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.529
in on itself.

00:15:55.529 --> 00:16:01.220
The entire expanded area collapsed into the
tiny space of the original altar room.

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:05.800
Through the rubble, the members of Zeta-9
found Richards’ journal along with a tiny

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:10.189
metal object - matching the descriptions of
SCP-184.

00:16:10.189 --> 00:16:13.139
They never did find Richards’ body.

00:16:13.139 --> 00:16:17.819
He went missing during the recovery, presumed
Killed in Action.

00:16:17.819 --> 00:16:21.939
After it was brought back to base, Foundation
researchers went to work on it.

00:16:21.939 --> 00:16:26.459
It was a tiny metal statuette in the shape
of a dodecahedron.

00:16:26.459 --> 00:16:31.870
The metal it was made from was unknown, but
tests revealed that it was magnetic and hard

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:33.149
as brass.

00:16:33.149 --> 00:16:34.449
Experiments followed.

00:16:34.449 --> 00:16:40.379
They discovered that when they put SCP-184
inside an enclosed structure, like a room

00:16:40.379 --> 00:16:46.759
or building or even a cardboard box, it would
expand the interior dimensions without making

00:16:46.759 --> 00:16:48.240
it grow larger.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:52.740
The effect was powerful - the rooms it was
tested in would grow by hundreds of square

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.589
meters every day.

00:16:54.589 --> 00:16:59.320
At first, it just moves the walls out, making
the room up to three times bigger than it

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:03.100
is – but after that, it gets strange.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:08.320
During a test in a small bedroom in a suburban
home, after it grew the room three times in

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:12.740
floor space, it began to create entirely new
rooms.

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:18.570
The researchers suddenly went in to find three
kitchens, six bedrooms, a dozen bathrooms,

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:20.339
and tens of closets.

00:17:20.339 --> 00:17:25.790
They were all fully furnished – SCP-184
was capable of copying materials from the

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:29.330
rest of the building, but not particularly
well.

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:33.690
The appliances in the kitchens were made of
wood or rock, and the ‘furniture’ was

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.620
limited to glass sofas and chairs.

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:41.420
The rooms were oddly-shaped as the house went
on – at first they were oval, but the deeper

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.990
bedrooms were pentagonal and even star-shaped.

00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:48.250
They even found one bathroom that was a perfect
sphere.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:52.820
Some of the doors led right into an empty
wall, and the hallways changed in size and

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:56.660
shape and led around into themselves like
a labyrinth.

00:17:56.660 --> 00:18:02.090
The researchers quickly removed SCP-184 from
the house and tried to figure out how to contain

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:03.090
this thing.

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:08.360
If there’s one thing the Foundation is good
at, it’s locking things up in boxes - but

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:14.020
locking this thing up in a box is the most
dangerous thing they could possibly do.

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:17.580
One researcher had an “out of the box”
idea.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:23.670
SCP-184 was placed between two electromagnets,
which kept it floating in mid-air and made

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.120
it impossible to pull away.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:30.900
That solved half the problem - and the Foundation
knew exactly where to put it without enclosing

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:32.210
it in a space.

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:37.160
Only a few years after the events of Zeta-9s
recovery, the Hong Kong government finally

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:42.640
demolished the massive Kowloon Walled City,
replacing it with an open park commemorating

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:46.730
the site, with many statuaries and relics
from the City.

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:52.380
The Foundation made sure they were able to
install SCP-184’s electromagnets as another

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:59.630
statuary inside a gazebo, finally containing
SCP-184 right where it had been all along.

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:05.830
Be it ever so humble, there’s no place like
eternally recursive home.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:12.900
Now go check out “SCP-3008 - Trapped in
IKEA” and “SCP-2427 - A Thing Full of

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:16.500
Stuff” for more anomalous locations you
might never escape!

